   <facsimile>
      <surface xml:id="pattern-page1">
         <graphic url="pulli.png"/>
         <!-- Add size and coordinates -->
         <zone xml:id="zone-back"/>
      </surface>
   </facsimile>
   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="document">
            <note ana="#adaptation" corresp="#infos" hand="#hand1">Nele, da sotto fino inizio ascella = 42 <lb/>Da inizio ascella a spalla dritto 18 obliquo 20</note>
            <note ana="#adaptation" hand="#hand1"><formula>62:108=21:x = 37</formula></note>
            
            <div type="infos" xml:id="infos">
               <p>
                  <hi rend="bold">MATERIALS</hi> One pair each Nod. 5 mm and 6 mm knitting pins. 4
                  markers. </p>

               <p>
                  <hi rend="bold">SIZES:</hi> 80 85 90 95 100 105 110 cm.</p>
               <p>50g balls: 18 18 19 21 22 24 25</p>
               
               <p>
                  <hi rend="bold">MEASUREMENTS:</hi>
                  Length of centre back below neckband:
                  68 68 69 72 73 76 76 cm.
                  Sleeve to armhole: 
                  46 47 48 49 50 51 52 cm.
                  <hi rend="bold">N.B.:</hi> Sleeve is 2 cm longer than normal to allow for deopped shoulders
               </p>
               
               <div type="diplomatic-transcription" xml:id="back-source">
                  <head><hi rend="bold">BACK:</hi></head>
                  <note ana="#adaptation" hand="#hand1" corresp="#cast-on-back"><hi rend="strikethrough">104</hi> <hi rend="strikethrough">113</hi> -> 107, perchè sennò non è divisibile</note>
                  <note ana="#adaptation" hand="#hand1" corresp="#cast-on-back">96 slighyly smaller or 102</note>
                  <p>With 5 mm pins <seg type="op" corresp="#cast-on-back">cast on 61 (67: 67: 73: 73: 79: 79) sts</seg> and <seg type ="op" corresp="#rib-back">work in rib</seg> as fol:</p>
                  <p><hi rend="bold">1st row:</hi>K1, *p1, k1, rep from * to end.</p>
                  <p><hi rend="bold">2nd row:</hi>P1, *k1, p1, rep from * to end.</p>
                  <p>Rep these 2 rows until work meas 6 cm, fin with a first row.</p><note ana="#specification" hand="#hand1" corresp="#rib-back">(17 rows)</note>
               </div>
               
               
               
               <div type="operational" xml:id="back-model">
  

                  <piece xml:id="piece-back" type="back">
                     <castOn xml:id="cast-on-back" count="61" unit="stitch"/>
                     <repeat xml:id="rib-back" count="6" unit="cm">
                        <!-- here my annotation says it's 17 rows. How to integrate documentary aspects as operations? -->

                        <row xml:id="row1" n="1" side="rs">
                           <stitch type="knit" count="1" consumes="1" produces="1" ana="#op-knit"/>
                           <repeat xml:id="rib-row1" count="to-end" unit="row">
                              <stitch type="purl" count="1" consumes="1" produces="1" ana="#op-purl"/>
                              <stitch type="knit" count="1" consumes="1" produces="1" ana="#op-knit"/>
                           </repeat>
                        </row>

                        <row xml:id="row2" n="2" side="ws">
                           <stitch type="purl" count="1" consumes="1" produces="1" ana="#op-purl"/>
                           <repeat xml:id="rib-row2" count="to-end" unit="row">
                              <stitch type="knit" count="1" consumes="1" produces="1" ana="#op-knit"/>
                              <stitch type="purl" count="1" consumes="1" produces="1" ana="#op-purl"/>
                           </repeat>
                        </row>

                     </repeat>


                     <row xml:id="rowBridge">
                        <!-- here again based on annotations I can say it is row 18 -->
                        <repeat corresp="#rib-row1 OR #rib-row2">
                           <!-- how to do this? -->
                           <!-- should I write this again?? -->
                           <!-- at half you need to increase 1 by lift one method  -->
                        </repeat>
                     </row>




                  </piece>
               </div>
            </div>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
</TEI>
